.TH LLAPI_FSWAP_LAYOUT_FIDS 3 2026-08-25 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_fswap_layout_fids \- exchange one OST object between two file layouts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_fswap_layout_fids(int " fd_src ", int " fd_volatile ,
.BI "                     const struct lu_fid *" fid_src ,
.BI "                     const struct lu_fid *" fid_volatile ,
.BI "                     __u64 " dv_src ", __u64 " dv_volatile ,
.BI "                     enum lustre_swap_layouts_flags " flags );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llapi_fswap_layout_fids()
atomically exchanges a single OST object between the layouts of two open
files identified by
.I fd_src
and
.IR fd_volatile .
The objects are selected by OST object FID
.RI ( fid_src
in the first file,
.I fid_volatile
in the second) rather than by layout index, so a concurrent component
delete/recreate cannot redirect the swap.
.PP
Typical use is surgical stripe migration: copy one stripe of a source file
into a partner (often a volatile file with a single stripe on the target
OST), then call
.B llapi_fswap_layout_fids()
to put the new object into the source layout. Multi-stripe partners are
allowed by the protocol as long as
.I fid_volatile
names the intended object. Same-OST partners are valid (e.g. repair a
corrupt object while remaining on that OST).
.PP
.I dv_src
and
.I dv_volatile
are file data versions captured around the data copy. The function always
ORs the following into the ioctl flags:
.TP
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_SINGLE_STRIPE
Exchange one object only; do not swap full layouts.
.TP
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_WITH_DV12
Transmit
.I dv_src
/
.I dv_volatile
to the MDS.
.TP
.BR SWAP_LAYOUTS_CHECK_DV1 " and " SWAP_LAYOUTS_CHECK_DV2
Return
.B -EAGAIN
if either file's data version changed since capture (source race or
volatile inconsistency).
.PP
Callers typically take
.I dv_src
before the data copy and
.I dv_volatile
after filling the partner.
.I flags
may carry additional
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_*
bits;
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_CLOSE
is rejected with
.BR -EINVAL .
.PP
Both descriptors must refer to regular files on a filesystem whose MDS
negotiated
.B OBD_CONNECT2_ONE_OBJ_SWAP .
Composite layouts including SEL (extension components) are supported;
only initialized components are searched for the FIDs.
.PP
The kernel only rejects a swap whose components have mismatched
.B lmm_stripe_size
(see
.B -EINVAL
below), since that is visible in the LOV metadata already in hand.
It does
.B not
verify that the two OST objects are the same length: object length is
stored on the OST, not the LOV, so checking it would require an extra
.BR getattr (2)
round trip. The caller is responsible for pairing objects of matching
length (e.g. by copying a full stripe's worth of data into the volatile
partner) so the file size does not change as a side effect of the swap.
The Size-on-MDT (SOM) cache, if any, is likewise left untouched by this
call.
.SH RETURN VALUES
.B llapi_fswap_layout_fids()
returns 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B -EINVAL
A FID is NULL or zero,
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_CLOSE
was requested, either file lacks a layout, the layout magic is
unrecognized, or the two OST objects being exchanged have different
.BR lmm_stripe_size .
.TP
.B -ENOENT
An FID was not found in the corresponding file layout.
.TP
.B -EPERM
The two files have different owners or groups.
.IP
For unprivileged callers, the two files' on-disk
.BR uid / gid
must match so a process that can open a foreign file for write cannot
launder another layout onto it.
.B Root is only exempt from this check for single-stripe FID swaps:
when
.B SWAP_LAYOUTS_SINGLE_STRIPE
is requested, callers with
.B CAP_FOWNER
(typically root) may replace a stripe across ownership without
.BR fchown (2)ing
a volatile partner first; the OST object is re-chowned to its new
file's owner as part of the swap so quota accounting stays correct.
A full layout swap
.RB ( SWAP_LAYOUTS_SINGLE_STRIPE
not set) still requires matching
.BR uid / gid
even for
.BR CAP_FOWNER
callers.
.B lfs migrate
and
.B lfs migrate_stripe
still fchown the partner for non-root paths.
.TP
.B -EAGAIN
A data version check failed; the source or volatile changed since the
versions were captured. Retry the copy and swap.
.TP
.B -EOPNOTSUPP
The MDS does not support single-stripe swap
.RB ( OBD_CONNECT2_ONE_OBJ_SWAP ).
.TP
.B -EBADF
.I fd_src
or
.I fd_volatile
is not a valid open file descriptor.
.TP
.B -ENOTTY
The file is not on a Lustre mount suitable for this ioctl.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
#include <lustre/lustreapi.h>

int fd_src, fd_volatile;
struct lu_fid fid_src, fid_volatile;
__u64 dv_src, dv_volatile;
int rc;

fd_src = open(path, O_RDWR | O_DIRECT);
/* create/open single-stripe volatile partner on the target OST */

rc = llapi_get_data_version(fd_src, &dv_src, LL_DV_RD_FLUSH);
/* copy the selected stripe from fd_src into fd_volatile */
rc = llapi_get_data_version(fd_volatile, &dv_volatile, LL_DV_RD_FLUSH);

/* resolve OST object FIDs for the stripe to exchange */
rc = llapi_fswap_layout_fids(fd_src, fd_volatile, &fid_src, &fid_volatile,
			      dv_src, dv_volatile, 0);
if (rc == -EAGAIN) {
	/* data version changed; retry copy and swap */
}
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_fswap_layout_fids()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.17.57.
